### Rule-Test Mapping
// IMPORTANT: Tests must be minimal and focused, affecting only the specific functionality being tested

1. Test File Organization:
   ```
   mobile/src/__tests__/battle/
   ├── core/              # @battle-core-mechanics.mdc tests
   │   ├── BattleCoreStats.test.ts
   │   └── BattleState.test.ts
   ├── movement/         # @battle-movement-system.mdc tests
   ├── targeting/        # @battle-targeting-system.mdc tests
   └── README.md        # Test status tracking
   ```

2. Test Implementation:
   ```typescript
   // Implementation of @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic#Battalion-Stats
   describe('Battalion Stats System', () => {
     it('should calculate correct stats', () => {
       // Minimal test focusing only on stats calculation
       const stats = calculateBattalionStats(BattalionType.Guardian, 1);
       expect(stats).toEqual({
         speed: 9,
         range: 4,
         // ... only test required properties
       });
     });
   });
   ```

3. Status Tracking:
   - [DONE] - Tests written and passing
   - [IN_PROGRESS] - Tests being implemented
   - [PENDING] - Tests not started
   - [BLOCKED] - Waiting on dependencies

### Test Focus Priority
1. Rule Implementation:
   - Test only what the rule requires
   - Keep tests minimal and focused
   - Avoid testing unrelated features
   - Document rule connections

2. Cross-Rule Testing:
   - Identify shared requirements
   - Test common functionality once
   - Reference all related rules
   - Maintain test independence

### Test Organization
1. File Structure:
   - Tests mirror rule organization
   - Group by battle system component
   - Keep setup minimal and focused
   - Document rule references

2. Naming Conventions:
   - Test files: `FeatureName.test.ts`
   - Rule reference in comments
   - Clear test descriptions
   - Status tracking in README

## Implementation Guidelines
// Implementation of @project-structure.mdc#Rule-Implementation-Strategy

1. Test First Development:
   ```typescript
   // Implementation of @battle-core-mechanics.mdc#Combat-Logic
   describe('Combat Calculations', () => {
     // Document rule requirements
     // Write minimal test
     // Implement only what's needed
     // Track completion status
   });
   ```

2. Test Scope:
   - Test only rule requirements
   - No unnecessary coverage
   - Clear rule references
   - Status documentation

3. Test Independence:
   - Tests don't affect each other
   - Minimal shared setup
   - Clean state between tests
   - Focused assertions

## Quality Gates
// Implementation of @project-structure.mdc#Quality-Gates

### Test Requirements
1. Must Have:
   - Rule reference comments
   - Minimal, focused tests
   - Clear status tracking
   - Independent execution
   - Full test suite validation after individual success

2. Must Not Have:
   - Unnecessary complexity
   - Unrelated test coverage
   - Cross-test dependencies
   - Duplicate rule testing

### Test Validation Process
1. Individual Test Phase:
   - Run specific test file
   - Validate all tests pass
   - Fix any failures
   - Document changes

2. Comprehensive Test Phase:
   - Run entire test suite
   - Verify no regressions
   - Check for side effects
   - Update status tracking

3. Test Commands:
   ```bash
   # Individual test
   npm test -- path/to/test.ts
   
   # Full test suite validation
   npm test
   ```

